## Unused local variables

```catala
#[test] declaration scope A:
  output a content integer
  output b content integer
  output c content integer
  output d content integer

declaration top content integer equals
  let dead_top equals 1 in
  2

scope A:
  definition a equals
    let dead equals 1 in
    2

  definition b equals
    let alive equals 40 in
    alive + top

  definition c equals
    let (kept, dropped) equals (1, 2) in
    kept

  definition d equals
    assertion (1 + 1 = 2) in
    if false then (let forced equals 1 in impossible) else 4
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope A
┌─[WARNING]─
│
│  The local variable "dead" is never used; maybe it's unnecessary?
│
├─➤ tests/name_resolution/good/unused_let_in.catala_en:16.9-13:
│    │
│ 16 │     let dead equals 1 in
│    │         ‾‾‾‾
└─ Unused local variables
┌─[WARNING]─
│
│  The local variable "dropped" is never used; maybe it's unnecessary?
│
├─➤ tests/name_resolution/good/unused_let_in.catala_en:24.16-23:
│    │
│ 24 │     let (kept, dropped) equals (1, 2) in
│    │                ‾‾‾‾‾‾‾
└─ Unused local variables
┌─[WARNING]─
│
│  The local variable "dead_top" is never used; maybe it's unnecessary?
│
├─➤ tests/name_resolution/good/unused_let_in.catala_en:11.7-15:
│    │
│ 11 │   let dead_top equals 1 in
│    │       ‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾
└─ Unused local variables
┌─[RESULT]─ A ─
│ a = 2
│ b = 42
│ c = 1
│ d = 4
└─
```
